1
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:04,670
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:32,840
[Ivan chuckles]
None of these people had to die

3
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:35,390
if Yuru had come alone
like I told him to.

4
00:01:35,890 --> 00:01:38,100
And these must
be the Divine Guardians.

5
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:39,600
Yuru's daemons.

6
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:41,980
What I don't get is
why the natural enemies

7
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,900
of Break and Seal would form
a contract with the twin.

8
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,610
Especially you, Left.

9
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:49,690
Your compatibility
with Seal couldn't be worse.

10
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,990
With you around,

11
00:01:52,110 --> 00:01:55,450
Seal might flat out refuse
to form a contract with Yuru.

12
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:58,120
Hate to say it, but...

13
00:01:59,750 --> 00:02:02,370
to ensure everything works out,
you gotta die.

14
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:03,670
[Right grunts]

15
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:06,540
The gentleman wants a duel!
What say you?

16
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:09,920
[LEFT] I gladly accept.

17
00:02:10,050 --> 00:02:12,590
Interesting.
From what I have observed,

18
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:15,470
swordsmen are a rarity
in these modern streets.

19
00:02:15,590 --> 00:02:18,350
Four centuries ago,
they darkened every doorway.

20
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:21,560
I should warn you that
there's more to these swords

21
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,640
than one might guess.

22
00:02:22,770 --> 00:02:24,230
Naturally.

23
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:26,940
That's why
I'll snap them in two.

24
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:37,160
[Left scoffs]

25
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,410
[Ivan exclaims softly]

26
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,330
[LEFT] Uh?

27
00:02:42,040 --> 00:02:43,120
[Left grunts]

28
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:48,880
[Dera grunts]

29
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:56,930
[DERA] Left, you're hurt!

30
00:02:57,050 --> 00:02:58,590
[LEFT] Calm yourself.

31
00:02:58,720 --> 00:03:01,180
You shall take me to the
home improvement merchant later.

32
00:03:01,310 --> 00:03:04,180
Yeah, sure, of course.
Because...

33
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:05,600
To fix this.

34
00:03:05,730 --> 00:03:08,060
They peddle adhesives made
for stone, yes?

35
00:03:08,190 --> 00:03:10,190
Hold up. That would heal you?

36
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:11,860
You forget that we are statues.

37
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:14,530
This will take some time
to repair,

38
00:03:14,650 --> 00:03:17,200
but losing an arm or two
shan't be the death of me.

39
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,700
[DERA] So reckless.

40
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:20,490
Isn't that a pain in the ass?

41
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:22,830
What is it going to take
to kill you?

42
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:24,710
It is you who are the pain!

43
00:03:24,830 --> 00:03:27,250
Those swords are sharp
and can regenerate.

44
00:03:27,540 --> 00:03:29,960
[sniffing]

45
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,250
Observe, Left.

46
00:03:32,710 --> 00:03:34,010
His katanas.

47
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:37,930
Do you smell it?
They reek of blood.

48
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:39,840
How are you surprised?

49
00:03:39,970 --> 00:03:41,760
He's surrounded by corpses.

50
00:03:41,890 --> 00:03:43,060
Mm?

51
00:03:43,260 --> 00:03:44,640
[grunts]

52
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,770
If my nose is to be believed,

53
00:03:46,890 --> 00:03:49,190
you've murdered an unbelievable
number of people.

54
00:03:49,690 --> 00:03:52,270
Well, a man's gotta
earn a living somehow.

55
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:54,530
I'll slice up anyone
for a check.

56
00:03:54,650 --> 00:03:58,160
Human or daemon, doesn't matter.
Whatever the job requires of me.

57
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,530
[Right sniffing]

58
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:01,990
I smell something else on you.

59
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:06,620
There's a relatively fresh blood
and blood from Higashi Village.

60
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:11,040
But beneath that,
a whisper of something else.

61
00:04:12,130 --> 00:04:14,920
A scent the two of us
are familiar with.

62
00:04:15,050 --> 00:04:16,630
It's Yuru's kin!

63
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:19,300
I smell the blood
of Mine and Nagisa!

64
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,270
[ASUMA]
So what do you say, Yuru?

65
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:31,150
Tell me, would it
please you to die?

66
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,610
Why? Do you intend to kill me?

67
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:37,070
I would be extremely grateful
if you made the choice for me.

68
00:04:37,190 --> 00:04:38,860
It'd save me a lot of trouble.

69
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:41,620
Did the head of the Kagemoris
order this?

70
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:45,330
[ASUMA] No. My thinking
doesn't align with my father's.

71
00:04:45,450 --> 00:04:48,960
The main Kagemori clan
is way too soft to be effective.

72
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,630
Oh, right, allow me
to introduce Shingo.

73
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,670
He's my mother's older brother.

74
00:04:55,500 --> 00:04:56,670
[Shingo grunts]

75
00:04:57,090 --> 00:05:00,590
You know, there's no place
for you in Higashi anymore.

76
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,680
[Yuru breathes shakily]

77
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:03,970
Your family got outta there
years ago.

78
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:05,470
And what did that get them?

79
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,230
The villagers you loved so much
tracked your sister down

80
00:05:08,350 --> 00:05:09,390
and killed her.

81
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:12,350
They've even tried to murder you
on a few occasions.

82
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:14,730
You don't owe these people
a thing.

83
00:05:14,860 --> 00:05:16,820
It's time to leave them behind.

84
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:17,900
[scoffs]

85
00:05:18,570 --> 00:05:21,650
Instead, you can join
the Shingo clan.

86
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:23,820
We could treat you very well.

87
00:05:23,950 --> 00:05:26,120
You mean the clan
that wants me dead?

88
00:05:26,240 --> 00:05:28,450
That went into the village
and kidnapped some kids

89
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,830
who must be terrified?

90
00:05:29,950 --> 00:05:31,000
We needed hostages,

91
00:05:31,120 --> 00:05:32,830
or else you wouldn't have
cooperated!

92
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:37,300
Don't worry, the fake Asa
and the kid are in a safe place

93
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:39,630
under watchful eyes, unharmed.

94
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:42,050
They're just
on a little vacation.

95
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:44,050
And yeah, of course
I would like it

96
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:45,470
if you kicked the bucket.

97
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,390
Seeing your corpse
would make my day.

98
00:05:47,510 --> 00:05:49,520
Perhaps phrase that differently?

99
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:53,140
But I'm gonna need you
to accept your death. Cool?

100
00:05:53,270 --> 00:05:54,480
What's cool about that?

101
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:57,520
[SHINGO] By the way,
you know the shaman, right?

102
00:05:57,650 --> 00:05:58,980
Mountain of a man?

103
00:05:59,110 --> 00:06:01,030
What? You mean Yama?

104
00:06:01,150 --> 00:06:02,780
He comes
to the village sometimes

105
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:03,950
to heal the sick.

106
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:07,200
If you're wondering who sent
the bandits to assassinate you,

107
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:08,370
it was him.

108
00:06:08,490 --> 00:06:09,490
[Yuru gasps]

109
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:11,950
[SHINGO] Tadera...
The guy who's supposed to be

110
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,210
looking out for you?

111
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:15,420
He hung out with the shaman
all the time.

112
00:06:15,540 --> 00:06:17,340
You can't trust him, either.

113
00:06:17,790 --> 00:06:20,050
Higashi Village kept
Seal a secret

114
00:06:20,170 --> 00:06:22,010
and waited for their chance
to kill you.

115
00:06:22,130 --> 00:06:23,180
If they'd had it their way,

116
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:25,130
you would have snuffed it
years ago.

117
00:06:25,260 --> 00:06:27,890
Don't give those fanatics
another spare thought.

118
00:06:28,010 --> 00:06:30,220
Instead, choose
to give up your own life.

119
00:06:30,350 --> 00:06:32,810
Let that damn village
crumble and die.

120
00:06:32,930 --> 00:06:33,940
[Yuru breathes shakily]

121
00:06:34,230 --> 00:06:37,060
[ASUMA] Please, Uncle,
I know how passionate you are,

122
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:39,360
but you shouldn't say
such things.

123
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:42,860
Everything in this world
serves some purpose.

124
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:44,440
[Yuru exhales]

125
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:48,620
[YURU] "A child like you
isn't needed in this world."

126
00:06:48,910 --> 00:06:52,330
[ASUMA] Yes. The village
that produces Break and Seal

127
00:06:52,450 --> 00:06:54,000
should be allowed to live on.

128
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,920
We mustn't reject their
very existence.

129
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:59,670
That's weird.
You don't agree with your uncle?

130
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:02,340
How does that work
if you're on the same side?

131
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:05,260
[ASUMA] Like Higashi Village
and the Kagemoris,

132
00:07:05,380 --> 00:07:07,430
there are
a number of differing opinions

133
00:07:07,550 --> 00:07:09,720
represented
within the Shingo Clan.

134
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,060
That's a positive thing.

135
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,730
It would be dangerous
for us to be

136
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,640
in total agreement
with one another.

137
00:07:15,770 --> 00:07:17,850
What the Shingo clan
is united on

138
00:07:17,980 --> 00:07:20,310
is the idea that
those who wield special powers

139
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:22,690
should be able to use them
without restraint.

140
00:07:22,820 --> 00:07:26,150
So long as they're overseen
by a responsible party.

141
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:28,950
There are plenty of perks
to joining us.

142
00:07:29,070 --> 00:07:31,700
The kind of support we can offer
will change your life.

143
00:07:31,830 --> 00:07:34,580
I'm talking money, resources.

144
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:36,370
Anything you might want.

145
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:42,170
[YURU] I already made my wishes
clear at the Kagemori mansion.

146
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:46,170
The only thing I want
is a normal life.

147
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:50,550
I want to hunt, farm,
cook over charcoal.

148
00:07:50,850 --> 00:07:52,060
Nothing special.

149
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:53,810
[Yozakura groans softly]

150
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:57,230
[YURU] I want to find
Mother and Father, too.

151
00:08:00,310 --> 00:08:01,560
Then...

152
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:03,690
there's Asa.

153
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:06,990
I don't know if she realizes
she's in a prison,

154
00:08:07,110 --> 00:08:08,740
but I want to free her from it.

155
00:08:10,410 --> 00:08:11,910
And one day soon,

156
00:08:12,030 --> 00:08:15,370
we'll all live an ordinary life
full of laughter together.

157
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:20,380
[RIGHT] Admit it. You murdered
Yuru's parents, didn't you?

158
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:22,500
And if you're not to blame,

159
00:08:22,630 --> 00:08:24,880
whoever was the master
of those sword daemons

160
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,010
before you spilled their blood.

161
00:08:27,130 --> 00:08:30,430
I can smell Mine and Nagisa
on those blades.

162
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:31,510
[Dera grunts]

163
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:33,550
[Ivan chuckles]

164
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,350
Who knows? I've cut down
so many people,

165
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:37,680
I can't remember them all.

166
00:08:37,810 --> 00:08:39,810
Don't dodge the question.

167
00:08:40,810 --> 00:08:43,150
[IVAN] Let's see what the swords
have to say.

168
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:46,400
-Dera, leave us and find Yuru.
-Uh?

169
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:50,400
[RIGHT] We'll take this man
and his daemons alive.

170
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:52,530
[LEFT] A gift for our master.

171
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,370
[DERA] You got it.

172
00:08:57,290 --> 00:08:58,790
Fool. Wasting shots.

173
00:08:58,910 --> 00:09:01,250
[DERA] I'm out!
See you later, sword pervert!

174
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:04,790
[IVAN] That bastard!

175
00:09:04,920 --> 00:09:06,420
He tricked me
into looking at the lights

176
00:09:06,550 --> 00:09:07,750
right before he killed them.

177
00:09:07,880 --> 00:09:10,920
My eyes aren't going to adjust
any time soon.

178
00:09:11,010 --> 00:09:12,430
Let me guess,

179
00:09:12,550 --> 00:09:14,470
Left and Right
use their sense of smell

180
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,930
to navigate the darkness.

181
00:09:16,050 --> 00:09:18,890
Ugh. How annoying.

182
00:09:19,810 --> 00:09:21,440
[loud crash]

183
00:09:22,270 --> 00:09:24,860
[DERA] Genius plan.
I said I'd look for Yuru,

184
00:09:24,980 --> 00:09:27,480
but I have no idea
where to start.

185
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:31,240
Is he even in this warehouse
district anymore?

186
00:09:31,360 --> 00:09:32,320
Uh?

187
00:09:34,740 --> 00:09:35,870
Wait, Tadera?

188
00:09:36,370 --> 00:09:38,620
Yeah. And you're a bandit.

189
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,120
-You hurt?
-I'll live,

190
00:09:41,250 --> 00:09:43,330
but the rest of my crew
wasn't so lucky.

191
00:09:43,790 --> 00:09:45,960
Did you meet the guy
with daemon swords?

192
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:48,670
[DERA] Yeah, I did.
Looked like bad news.

193
00:09:48,800 --> 00:09:51,300
What the heck are you
even doing here, Tadera?

194
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,880
We made sure
that you wouldn't know

195
00:09:53,010 --> 00:09:54,390
anything about this job.

196
00:09:54,510 --> 00:09:56,890
I bet that gravedigger
couldn't keep her mouth shut!

197
00:09:57,010 --> 00:09:59,850
Who? You mean Hana?
She's a steel trap.

198
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:02,520
One of your bandits
has been leaking info to me

199
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:04,440
on the side for a while now.

200
00:10:04,560 --> 00:10:07,110
Didn't make it outta
that warehouse, though.

201
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:11,320
Ah, damn it. You just can't rely
on anyone these days.

202
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,360
[DERA] Dead men tell no tales.

203
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:17,080
Yuru came to rescue the fake Asa
and the kid from the village,

204
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:19,540
but got taken by a daemon
that looked like a crow.

205
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:22,040
[BANDIT] He's been kidnapped?
Are you an idiot?

206
00:10:22,160 --> 00:10:23,750
Why would you bring him here?

207
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:27,460
Seems like just about
everybody wants the twins dead.

208
00:10:27,590 --> 00:10:31,000
And Yuru, that kid's desperate
to find something he can trust.

209
00:10:31,550 --> 00:10:34,930
He figured out you bandits
were trying to assassinate him.

210
00:10:35,050 --> 00:10:36,720
You can imagine
how he took that.

211
00:10:36,840 --> 00:10:39,310
Hey. You were
on our side first, Tadera.

212
00:10:39,430 --> 00:10:41,310
Did you forget?
Don't start pretending

213
00:10:41,430 --> 00:10:44,230
-you care about that boy.
-[DERA] Yeah, good point.

214
00:10:44,350 --> 00:10:46,610
I've been keeping secrets
from him, too.

215
00:10:46,730 --> 00:10:49,020
I don't expect Yuru
to fully trust me.

216
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:50,820
He's got no reason to.

217
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:53,990
The thing is, we've bonded.

218
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:56,910
In the past, I could ignore
some parts of my job.

219
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:59,530
But lately, it seems I've had
a change of heart.

220
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:01,700
So you're betraying
Higashi Village?

221
00:11:01,830 --> 00:11:03,460
I'm not betraying anybody.

222
00:11:04,040 --> 00:11:06,870
If you promise to back off
and leave Yuru alone,

223
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,960
I'll have no reason
to fight with you.

224
00:11:09,090 --> 00:11:11,090
They're the first twins
in 400 years.

225
00:11:11,210 --> 00:11:13,050
If they had their hands
on Break and Seal,

226
00:11:13,170 --> 00:11:15,880
Higashi Village could conquer
the entire world with ease.

227
00:11:16,010 --> 00:11:16,880
[Dera grunts]

228
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,760
I don't want to end up
an old man

229
00:11:18,890 --> 00:11:20,760
thinking about
how I got ahead in my life

230
00:11:20,890 --> 00:11:23,980
by sacrificing two
innocent children. Understand?

231
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:25,730
[bandit grunts]

232
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:30,570
[breathes uneasily]

233
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:33,070
[sighs]

234
00:11:34,190 --> 00:11:37,660
We can argue about this later.
Let's look for Yuru.

235
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,660
[Dera grunts]

236
00:11:40,330 --> 00:11:42,490
After I saw the message
about this warehouse,

237
00:11:42,620 --> 00:11:44,500
I did some digging
to see who owned it.

238
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:45,700
Find anything?

239
00:11:46,370 --> 00:11:48,460
[BANDIT]
It belongs to TT Logistics.

240
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:50,920
Their parent company
is Shingo Shipping.

241
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:54,420
There's a Shingo clan
that's related to the Kagemoris.

242
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:56,590
You know Gonzo's second kid,
Asuma?

243
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:58,510
They're his family
on the mom's side.

244
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:00,680
I looked into every business
I could find

245
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,350
connected to the Shingos.

246
00:12:02,470 --> 00:12:05,480
TT Logistics,
Kibushi Industries.

247
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,600
Plenty more.

248
00:12:06,730 --> 00:12:08,440
[DERA] Whoa,
that's one hell of a list.

249
00:12:08,560 --> 00:12:10,650
Are we gonna have to search
all of them?

250
00:12:10,770 --> 00:12:13,150
No way. If Yuru was kidnapped
by a daemon,

251
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:15,730
my guess is it'll still be
standing guard over him.

252
00:12:16,190 --> 00:12:18,200
We'll hunt daemons with daemons.

253
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:19,280
[both exclaim]

254
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,870
[BANDIT] These are mine,
Mamegarasu.

255
00:12:21,990 --> 00:12:23,490
[BOW-LEGS] I'm Bow-Legs.

256
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:24,990
[PIGEON-TOES] I'm Pigeon-Toes.

257
00:12:25,120 --> 00:12:26,830
Hi, good to meet you.

258
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:30,630
[BANDIT] I want you to help us
locate any daemons nearby.

259
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,880
[BOTH] Happy to be of service.

260
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,340
[BANDIT] You don't have
any daemons of your own?

261
00:12:35,460 --> 00:12:37,840
Nah, I'm pretty useless
on that front.

262
00:12:37,970 --> 00:12:39,470
[BANDIT] If you can see them,

263
00:12:39,590 --> 00:12:41,800
then you must've had
some in the past.

264
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:43,100
So what's the issue?

265
00:12:43,260 --> 00:12:45,640
You're not going to form
a contract with a new pair?

266
00:12:45,760 --> 00:12:47,390
[BOTH] So sad!

267
00:12:47,520 --> 00:12:48,600
[Dera sighs]

268
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:52,860
Well, maybe one day,
if I get the chance.

269
00:12:55,730 --> 00:12:57,690
♪

270
00:13:00,070 --> 00:13:03,120
[clanging]

271
00:13:03,700 --> 00:13:05,580
[sword swooshing]

272
00:13:07,330 --> 00:13:09,160
[Right grunting]

273
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:15,250
[Ivan sighs]

274
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:18,000
[IVAN] I'm finally adjusting
to the dark.

275
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:20,130
[SHOKYO]
Quit wasting time, monkey.

276
00:13:20,260 --> 00:13:22,220
They're making this harder
than it needs to be

277
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:24,140
by trying to capture me alive.

278
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,180
Their attacks
would be easier to read

279
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:28,560
if they were actually going
for the kill.

280
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:31,770
I only remember throwing down
the gauntlet to Left!

281
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:33,560
Turning this into
a two versus one

282
00:13:33,690 --> 00:13:34,610
hardly seems fair!

283
00:13:34,900 --> 00:13:36,940
You'll make your master cry
acting like this.

284
00:13:37,070 --> 00:13:38,900
Where's your honor?
Your humanity?

285
00:13:39,030 --> 00:13:40,530
[RIGHT] We're not humans.

286
00:13:40,650 --> 00:13:42,490
[LEFT] And Yuru won't mind.

287
00:13:42,610 --> 00:13:43,570
[Ivan grunts]

288
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:44,870
[IVAN] These brutes.

289
00:13:45,450 --> 00:13:47,790
I'd like to take this outside,

290
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,620
but with them blocking
either exit,

291
00:13:49,750 --> 00:13:51,500
that'll be a trial of its own.

292
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:54,290
They want me with
limited space to move.

293
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:59,250
Ah, crap. Shouldn't have left
these bodies lying around.

294
00:13:59,380 --> 00:14:01,720
They're tripping hazards
in the dark.

295
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:04,590
Why don't we take this outside?

296
00:14:10,350 --> 00:14:12,930
You should treat the dead
with a bit more care.

297
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:26,370
[Ivan exclaims]

298
00:14:26,990 --> 00:14:29,330
[IVAN]
Look at that beautiful moon.

299
00:14:30,750 --> 00:14:32,710
Unless our master
should spare you,

300
00:14:32,830 --> 00:14:35,960
this full moon may be your last.
Savor it.

301
00:14:37,290 --> 00:14:38,590
Well said.

302
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:41,050
I hope you take your own words
to heart.

303
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:42,470
[Left gasps]

304
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,640
[RIGHT] Left, watch out!

305
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:50,810
[grunts]

306
00:14:55,560 --> 00:14:57,980
You had my back. Thank you.

307
00:14:58,110 --> 00:15:00,270
You're damn right I did.

308
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,570
If your goal's "defeat Left,"

309
00:15:02,690 --> 00:15:04,860
you'd best be ready
to get through me first.

310
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:06,280
Is that the case?

311
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,620
Fine!

312
00:15:07,740 --> 00:15:09,080
[Right grunting]

313
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:18,500
I suppose that's what they call
losing the battle

314
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:19,540
to win the war?

315
00:15:20,670 --> 00:15:22,130
[Right grunting]

316
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:32,680
[RIGHT] He's evading our attacks
by a hair's breadth!

317
00:15:33,730 --> 00:15:35,980
[LEFT] He's learned
our ranges perfectly.

318
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:37,190
[Right grunts]

319
00:15:38,350 --> 00:15:40,730
[IVAN] A left hook.
With her reach,

320
00:15:40,860 --> 00:15:43,110
a half step back
will be enough to dodge.

321
00:15:43,230 --> 00:15:45,990
Then I'll counter
by taking her other arm.

322
00:15:51,330 --> 00:15:55,120
What kind of madwoman would use
her own severed arm as a weapon?

323
00:15:58,210 --> 00:15:59,630
[Ivan sighs]

324
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,670
This is starting
to get too much for me. [spits]

325
00:16:02,790 --> 00:16:05,670
[Shokyo scoffs]
Weak flesh bag! Push yourself!

326
00:16:05,800 --> 00:16:08,090
[IVAN] Need I remind you
my right leg is wounded

327
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:10,050
from where you stabbed it,
Shokyo?

328
00:16:10,180 --> 00:16:12,640
[SHOKYO] You monkeys
should regenerate faster!

329
00:16:12,760 --> 00:16:15,640
-[DAIKYO] Ivan.
-Whoa, you spoke up?

330
00:16:15,770 --> 00:16:17,140
What's the occasion, Daikyo?

331
00:16:17,270 --> 00:16:19,600
[DAIKYO] Something has arrived.

332
00:16:19,730 --> 00:16:20,770
[IVAN] Hmm?

333
00:16:21,230 --> 00:16:23,860
[DAIKYO]
Something really bad is here.

334
00:16:24,900 --> 00:16:26,440
[MAN 1]
You should have been there.

335
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:28,030
[chuckles]

336
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:29,530
[MAN 2] No way that's real.

337
00:16:29,650 --> 00:16:31,950
[MAN 1] I swear, I'm serious.
Think I'd lie?

338
00:16:32,070 --> 00:16:33,080
[GONZO] Hello.

339
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:34,370
[BOTH] Mm?

340
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:38,620
Quick question, gentlemen.

341
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:40,630
Is this the office
of Shingo Shipping,

342
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,080
by any chance?

343
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:43,670
[BOTH] Afraid not!

344
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:46,130
Sorry, but we're
Kibushi Industries.

345
00:16:46,250 --> 00:16:47,170
[line ringing]

346
00:16:47,470 --> 00:16:49,550
[GONZO] Ah, but isn't that
a Shingo subsidiary?

347
00:16:49,670 --> 00:16:52,260
[MAN 1] I wouldn't know.
I'm just a part-timer.

348
00:16:52,390 --> 00:16:54,350
I don't keep up
with that corporate stuff.

349
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,560
-[Gonzo laughs]
-[MAN 2] Hey.

350
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:56,770
-Send some guys.
-[GONZO] Don't play dumb.

351
00:16:56,890 --> 00:16:58,680
[MAN 2] Looks like
Gonzo Kagemori's...

352
00:17:00,940 --> 00:17:02,100
[GONZO] Go on.

353
00:17:02,230 --> 00:17:03,480
[whimpers]

354
00:17:03,610 --> 00:17:05,980
[GONZO] I didn't mean
to interrupt your call.

355
00:17:06,230 --> 00:17:09,030
[squeaking]

356
00:17:13,370 --> 00:17:15,080
Send your friends over!

357
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,540
I'll take on
every last one of you.

358
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:19,540
[both trembling]

359
00:17:19,910 --> 00:17:21,670
[BANDIT]
What's wrong, little guys?

360
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:24,250
Why'd they start trembling
out of the blue?

361
00:17:24,380 --> 00:17:25,800
[Dera gasps]

362
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:26,960
[both trembling]

363
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,880
[DERA] Seems like
something real nasty

364
00:17:30,010 --> 00:17:31,420
just showed up.

365
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:33,130
[grunting]

366
00:17:40,430 --> 00:17:42,850
[MAN] Who is this old man?

367
00:17:42,980 --> 00:17:45,820
Get away! Gramps here
is a Daemon Wielder!

368
00:17:45,940 --> 00:17:47,150
Oh, Hebota!

369
00:17:47,270 --> 00:17:48,940
I am seriously glad
to see you, man!

370
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:51,360
You guys don't stand a chance
against him.

371
00:17:51,490 --> 00:17:52,490
You wanna fight daemons?

372
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:54,910
Then you're gonna need
some daemons of your own.

373
00:17:55,030 --> 00:17:56,530
Now go, my...

374
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:58,660
[gasps]

375
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:02,960
[gasps]

376
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,960
-[screams]
-[BOTH] No, Hebota!

377
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:07,500
Wait, what?

378
00:18:07,630 --> 00:18:09,130
I can't tell what's going on.

379
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:12,050
Anyone here with daemons,
team up to take down Grandpa.

380
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:14,680
[MAN 1] Great.
How can we do that?

381
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,300
[growling]

382
00:18:16,430 --> 00:18:18,060
[MAN 2] The geezer's got
more pairs of ‘em

383
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:19,470
than I can count!

384
00:18:20,970 --> 00:18:22,890
[all screaming]

385
00:18:26,150 --> 00:18:27,690
[rumbling]

386
00:18:28,650 --> 00:18:30,570
[humming]

387
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:32,400
[rumbling]

388
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:36,030
Hmm. That is a lot of noise.
Wonder...

389
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,910
[screams]

390
00:18:41,490 --> 00:18:43,710
[Gonzo grunting]

391
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:52,130
[GUARD] Some random old dude
is out there shadow boxing.

392
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:56,260
And every time he swings,
something explodes.

393
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,640
♪

394
00:18:58,100 --> 00:18:59,680
Hello, headquarters?

395
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:02,310
I seem to be hallucinating.
Can I have a break?

396
00:19:02,430 --> 00:19:04,480
[MALE HQ] What?
Quit screwing around

397
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:06,190
and get back to work.

398
00:19:07,270 --> 00:19:09,690
[guard cries] I hate this job!

399
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,190
[rumbling]

400
00:19:14,650 --> 00:19:16,150
[footsteps]

401
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:20,240
[DERA] What? Is that the head
of the Kagemori clan?

402
00:19:20,370 --> 00:19:21,620
You mean Gonzo's here?

403
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:23,660
Of course my guys
are freaked out!

404
00:19:23,790 --> 00:19:25,330
They're sensing
a mansion's worth of daemons.

405
00:19:25,460 --> 00:19:26,580
Who wouldn't be?

406
00:19:26,710 --> 00:19:29,880
Awesome. How are we
supposed to find Yuru now?

407
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,250
♪

408
00:19:31,380 --> 00:19:32,420
[RIGHT] Huh?

409
00:19:32,550 --> 00:19:34,010
What are we sensing?

410
00:19:34,130 --> 00:19:36,220
-[IVAN] Hmm.
-If I did not know better,

411
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:38,890
I'd say the Kagemori manor
itself sprouted legs

412
00:19:39,010 --> 00:19:40,260
and walked here.

413
00:19:44,100 --> 00:19:45,350
[HAGURE] You've got it!

414
00:19:45,480 --> 00:19:47,440
Just fill in all the spots
I marked with an X!

415
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,360
So, is this okay?

416
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:52,400
Perfect! Very precise.
You've got steady hands!

417
00:19:52,520 --> 00:19:55,030
Now, where's
Miss "Zero Artistic Talent?"

418
00:19:55,150 --> 00:19:57,650
You ask me, I'd say
you have a real knack for this!

419
00:19:57,780 --> 00:20:00,030
Aw, I don't know about that.

420
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:01,830
Well, I'm gonna go take a bath,

421
00:20:01,950 --> 00:20:04,040
so please just keep
doing what you're doing.

422
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,950
Aye, aye. [giggles]

423
00:20:06,250 --> 00:20:07,500
[chuckles]

424
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:10,170
[door opens, closes]

425
00:20:11,960 --> 00:20:14,670
[TACHIKAWA] Wait a sec,
how exactly did I get here?

426
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:18,050
How did a merc like me wind up
spot-filling for a mangaka?

427
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:19,590
[ASA] I want to see my brother.

428
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:22,100
What are you thinking, Asa?

429
00:20:22,220 --> 00:20:24,220
Could you see yourself
being Hagure's assistant

430
00:20:24,350 --> 00:20:25,520
for the rest of your life?

431
00:20:25,640 --> 00:20:27,390
Or is there anything else
you want?

432
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:28,980
I want to see my brother.

433
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:30,480
Oh, right.

434
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,650
[phone vibrating]

435
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:37,740
-[TACHIKAWA] Hello?
-I want to see my brother.

436
00:20:37,860 --> 00:20:40,160
Hold on, let me step outside
real quick.

437
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,910
It's a little noisy in here.

438
00:20:42,870 --> 00:20:44,740
Yeah, I'm at work right now.

439
00:20:45,080 --> 00:20:47,000
Yeah, everything
will be all right.

440
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:50,080
I figured out how we can deal
with all Mom's hospital bills.

441
00:20:50,210 --> 00:20:51,790
Let your big sister handle it.

442
00:20:51,920 --> 00:20:53,840
♪

443
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:00,430
Hey, Gabby, why don't we
take a break, also?

444
00:21:01,010 --> 00:21:02,640
Right. Forgot.

445
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:04,430
She had a job to do.

446
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:08,230
Oh, wow, you're all by yourself.

447
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:09,810
Ms. Gabby's so protective,

448
00:21:09,930 --> 00:21:11,770
she's normally stuck to you
like glue.

449
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:13,980
This is a rare sight, isn't it?

450
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:16,030
I suppose so.

451
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,280
You should be careful
not to let your guard down

452
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,690
when you're alone.

453
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:22,820
You never know when some more
assassins could sneak in here.

454
00:21:22,950 --> 00:21:25,080
How about I stay
to keep you safe?

455
00:21:25,830 --> 00:21:27,540
Hey, Akio?

456
00:21:27,990 --> 00:21:29,290
You look strange.

457
00:21:29,410 --> 00:21:31,250
Are you hiding something?

458
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,880
Akio?

459
00:21:37,090 --> 00:21:40,170
Uh, no. I'm actually fine
by myself.

460
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:44,510
I said I'm okay. Hold on. Stop!

461
00:21:45,350 --> 00:21:47,100
You'd better back up!

462
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:49,020
[breathes uneasily]

463
00:21:50,390 --> 00:21:52,640
'Cause if you get closer...

464
00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:57,440
[♪ closing theme song playing]

465
00:23:27,820 --> 00:23:29,240
[GONZO] What a haul we've got!

466
00:23:29,370 --> 00:23:31,370
[GABBY] Pretty sure
I made it crystal clear

467
00:23:31,490 --> 00:23:34,080
when we first met
which one of us is stronger!

468
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,290
[AKIO] How unfortunate.

469
00:23:35,410 --> 00:23:37,540
I hate it when women lie.
